title: Login page fetches the victim's brand logo
severity: high
score: 50
tags: phishing, credential-harvest
attack: T1566.002, T1656
description: A password page fetches another site's favicon through a favicon service
  (Google s2/faviconV2, DuckDuckGo, Clearbit). Webmail kits use this trick to show the
  victim's own mail-provider icon. The page also is on free hosting, is on a domain under 30
  days old, calls an IP-lookup service or shows verification wording.
---
// A password page ...
password_pages
// ... that fetches the favicon of one to three other sites through a favicon service
// (the visitor's own mail provider's logo) ...
| extend favicons = toscalar(favicon_lookups | where not(visited) | summarize dcount(target))
| where favicons > 0 and favicons <= 3
// ... on a free-hosted or young domain, with an IP lookup or verification wording.
| where exists(final_free_hosting)
    or toscalar(final_domain | project age_days) < 30
    or exists(ip_lookups)
    or exists(verification_texts)
| project url, favicon_targets = toscalar(favicon_lookups | where not(visited) | summarize make_set(target))
